18:["$","section",null,{"className":"paper-section","id":"generated","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Generated-video experiments"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"prose","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["The matched diagnostic contains ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"12 T2 sequence clips and 30 T3 cup-shuffle clips"}],". Every method receives the same clip identifiers, but uses its own observation-selection and inference path. These experiments evaluate memory readout and high-level command generation. They do not execute G0.5 or measure physical manipulation success."]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"prose","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Models used in this comparison"}],["$","p",null,{"children":["Both video baselines use frozen ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct"}]," for high-level reasoning. The no-memory VLM is labeled “Vanilla G0.5” in the paper’s diagnostic table; ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"G0.5 motor inference is not run on passive videos"}],"."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"model-notes","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"No-memory"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct · final frame only"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Memory baseline (HiMe)"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct · episodic and procedural memory"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"REMM"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["T2: Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct + event memory",["$","br",null,{}],"T3: MIL identity tracking + task compiler"]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"diagnostic-videos","children":[["$","figure",null,{"children":[["$","video",null,{"controls":true,"playsInline":true,"preload":"none","poster":"/videos/generated-sequence.jpg","aria-label":"Generated T2 ordered-sequence diagnostic example","children":["$","source",null,{"src":"/videos/generated-sequence.mp4","type":"video/mp4"}]}],["$","figcaption",null